  "final_text": "I fixed the bug in `invoicing/currency.py`. The full test suite now passes (8 tests), including `test_invoice_jpy`.\n\n**The bug:** `minor_units()` converted the currency code to lowercase (`currency.lower()`) before checking it against `ZERO_DECIMAL`, but that set holds uppercase codes (`{\"JPY\", \"KRW\"}`). The check never matched, so JPY was treated as having 2 decimal places. That made the conversion 100\u00d7 too large, and the amount was then shown with decimals: `\u00a514,118.50` instead of `\u00a514,118`.\n\n**The fix:** I changed `currency.lower()` to `currency.upper()`. Zero-decimal currencies are now rec"
